@@ -70,7 +70,7 @@ Friedrich Nietzsche saw what was at stake more clearly than almost anyone, and h
 
 He was right about more than the English. Much of what modern people take to be plain decency was not plain to the ancient world. The conviction that a slave, an unwanted newborn or a foreigner has the same worth as a senator's son was not the common sense of Rome. The church carried it into that world because it believed every human being bears the image of God. The Bible grounds the prohibition of murder there, in the covenant with Noah: "Whoever sheds the blood of man, by man shall his blood be shed, for God made man in his own image" (Genesis 9:6).
 
-The early Christians acted on that belief long before they had any power. Where abandoning an unwanted newborn was common and accepted, they refused to abandon their own, and Justin told the emperor so. The secular person who takes the equal dignity of every human being for granted is still drawing on that inheritance, whether or not he would put it that way.
+The early Christians acted on that belief long before they had any power. Where abandoning an unwanted newborn was common and accepted, they refused to abandon their own, and [Justin told the emperor so](/writing/the-children-rome-threw-away). The secular person who takes the equal dignity of every human being for granted is still drawing on that inheritance, whether or not he would put it that way.
 
 An unbeliever has two replies to this. Many secular people have kept that conviction with great faithfulness, and a person doesn't need the theology to love his neighbor. And Christians have kept the theology while betraying it in practice more often than we like to remember, in [the slavery our preachers defended from the pulpit](/writing/why-didnt-the-bible-ban-slavery) and in churches that protected their own reputation at the expense of the people they had harmed. Both replies are true.
 
diff --git a/docs/work/essays/is-it-wrong-to-love-your-country.md b/docs/work/essays/is-it-wrong-to-love-your-country.md
